<article class="env-lemma" id="01NG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01NG">Lemma <span data-tag="01NG">27.13.3</span>.</a> Projective $n$-space over $\mathbf{Z}$ is covered by $n + 1$ standard opens </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathbf{P}^ n_{\mathbf{Z}} = \bigcup \nolimits _{i = 0, \ldots , n} D_{+}(T_ i)  \]
</div>
  <p> where each $D_{+}(T_ i)$ is isomorphic to $\mathbf{A}^ n_{\mathbf{Z}}$ affine $n$-space over $\mathbf{Z}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $\mathbf{Z}[T_0, \ldots , T_ n]_{+} = (T_0, \ldots , T_ n)$ and since 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}\left( \mathbf{Z} \left[\frac{T_0}{T_ i}, \ldots , \frac{T_ n}{T_ i} \right] \right) \cong \mathbf{A}^ n_{\mathbf{Z}}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       in an obvious way. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>